# input3.sscript -- consumed by bootstrap3.exe.
#
# bootstrap3 is a tiny SemanticScript-written compiler. It reads this file,
# locates the marker token `ExitCode`, parses the integer literal that
# follows on the same line, and emits LLVM IR for a program that returns
# that integer from main(). The literal here is therefore the exit code
# the resulting executable will produce when run.
#
# Supported SemanticScript subset (bootstrap3):
#   - project / target / runtime / entry / operation headers (parsed by the
#     reference compiler, ignored by bootstrap3 itself)
#   - label startMain
#   - const NAME ExitCode <integer literal>
#   - returnOk NAME
#
# Anything else in the file is treated as comment-equivalent by bootstrap3.

project Tiny3
target console
runtime AgentRuntime 0.1
entry console main

operation main
output main Result ExitCode MainError
effect main exit process
memory main heap no
async main no
purpose main "Trivial constant-return program: exit with the literal below."

label startMain

const exitCodeValue ExitCode 42
returnOk exitCodeValue
